<header class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>Funding and independence</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      The EISS is funded by its members. This page sets out where the money comes from, what our
      legal status is, and how the European funding acknowledged on our conference pages relates
      to it.
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <dl class="definition-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Membership fees</dt>
        <dd>
          Membership fees are what the association runs on. We take no core funding from
          governments, companies or foundations.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>No salaried staff</dt>
        <dd>
          Everyone here is a volunteer, the board included. The network has no payroll, and the
          people who organise the conference and maintain the Anthology are not paid for it.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>A French association <em lang="fr">loi 1901</em></dt>
        <dd>
          Registered under number W751263001 in the
          <span lang="fr">Répertoire National des Associations</span>, within the
          <span lang="fr">économie sociale et solidaire</span>. The registration is public and can
          be checked against that number.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>European funding, and what it covers</h2>
    <p style="max-width: 44rem;">
      Our conference pages carry an acknowledgement of European Union funding. It belongs to the
      COST Action, not to the EISS:
    </p>

    <article class="card" style="padding: clamp(var(--space-5), 2vw + 1rem, var(--space-6)); max-width: 44rem;">
      <p class="muted" style="margin: 0;">
        The Networking European Security Knowledge (NetSec) COST Action (CA24154) is supported by
        the Horizon Programme of the European Union.
      </p>
    </article>

    <p style="max-width: 44rem; margin-top: var(--space-5);">
      That funding supports NetSec and the joint European Security Studies Conference held with it.
      It does not fund the EISS's own running costs, which is why it appears on the pages for those
      events and not here. The
      <a href="{{ '/2026.html' | localizedHref(lang) }}">2026 conference page</a> carries the
      acknowledgement in full, as each conference page does.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="card" style="display: grid; gap: var(--space-5); grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: clamp(var(--space-6), 2vw + 1rem, var(--space-8));">
